message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Female Reservation and the Qualifications of Local Elected Officials in India"
abstract: >-
  Compares winners of women-reserved and open seats in rural councils in
  Bihar, Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan and Kerala and in the municipal councils of
  Mumbai and Delhi. Reserved-seat village heads in Bihar and Uttar Pradesh are
  much less likely to hold a degree; Kerala's council members and urban
  councillors show no lower graduate share, and urban reserved-seat winners
  are less likely to face pending criminal cases.
authors:
